# Line endings. This project is authored on Linux and runs CI on Linux; Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true,
# which would rewrite text files to CRLF in a Windows clone. Anything that hashes file bytes (vendored libraries with SRI
# in public/assets/vendor/, dataset and fixture checks) then fails. Keep text as LF everywhere, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored third-party files are integrity-pinned (SHA-256 / SRI): Git must never touch a single byte of them.
public/assets/vendor/** -text

# Binary files (a self-checking test, tests/backend/test_gitattributes.py, fails if a new binary type is not listed here).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.joblib binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pdf binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.sqlite binary
*.db binary
*.zip binary
*.wasm binary
